Title:
Soaphound.py — BloodHound Python Ingestor using ADWS

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Soaphound.py is a Python-based BloodHound data collector designed to enumerate Active Directory primarily over ADWS (Active Directory Web Services), making it useful from Linux without relying solely on LDAP for object collection. It aims to collect “most valuable” object data by applying per-object logic similar to BloodHound.py/SharpHound approaches, and can optionally enumerate remote session information (SMB-based) like BloodHound.py. It supports NTLM (password or NT hash) and Kerberos authentication via ccache (KRB5CCNAME), with an ADWS-only mode to avoid computer connection/session collection. The tool also includes optional AD CS enumeration (“cert-find”) similar to Certipy, including web enrollment probing and optional CA enrichment via RPC/Remote Registry. Recent development adds deeper GPO/SYSVOL parsing (e.g., Groups.xml, GptTmpl.inf, privilege rights) and GPP cpassword decryption to surface impactful policy-driven access changes. It’s primarily useful for red teams and pentesters building BloodHound graphs from non-Windows hosts, and for defenders validating AD exposure paths via ADWS/GPO/ADCS visibility.

Technical Focus:
- Active Directory Web Services (ADWS) enumeration (MS-ADDM / SOAP/NBFX)
- BloodHound-compatible JSON collection/ingestion workflows
- NTLM and Kerberos auth (ccache, AES keys) for ADWS/SMB operations
- SMB-based remote session enumeration
- AD CS discovery (templates, CAs, web enrollment probing/EPA handling)
- GPO + SYSVOL parsing (GptTmpl.inf, Groups.xml), GPP cpassword decryption

Use Cases:
- Collect BloodHound datasets from Linux in environments where LDAP collection is constrained or monitored
- Perform stealthier/alternative AD enumeration via ADWS endpoints on domain controllers
- Enumerate user sessions and computer relationships to support lateral movement planning
- Identify risky GPO-driven configurations (local admins, RDP/DCOM/PSRemoting rights) via SYSVOL artifacts
- Enumerate AD CS configuration and templates to assess certificate-based escalation paths

Keywords:
Soaphound.py, BloodHound, SharpHound, BloodHound.py, Active Directory, ADWS, MS-ADDM, SOAP, NBFX, Kerberos, NTLM, ccache, KRB5CCNAME, SMB, session enumeration, SYSVOL, GPO, GPP cpassword, AD CS, Certipy find, WMI filters, gPLink, Remote Registry, RPC